    "title": "Depth-first search: stack, deep dive and backtracking",
    "subject": "Computer Science",
    "topic": "Depth-First Search",
    "objective": "Show DFS visiting a branch deeply before backtracking.",
    "learner": "Knows stacks/graphs.",
    "misconceptions": [
      "DFS visits level by level",
      "Backtracking is a new search"
    ],
    "expectedUnderstanding": "DFS keeps the current path on a stack, pushes a node when it moves to it, and only pops when every neighbour is already visited; the pops are backtracking along the same search, and the first route found can be much longer than the shortest one."
  },
